{
  "_comment": [
    "Maps this module's clinical fields onto concepts, so the observation projector can write",
    "them into the core OpenMRS model, where the FHIR2 module can see them.",
    "",
    "patientview gains NO dependency on fhir2 from this file or from the code that reads it.",
    "The projector calls only ObsService, EncounterService, ConceptService and ConditionService",
    "- core platform APIs. FHIR2 reads the core model on its own. That indirection is what",
    "makes this survive an fhir2 major upgrade: the one thing that has broken downstream",
    "modules across fhir2 majors is its DAO layer, which nothing here touches.",
    "",
    "CONCEPTS ARE REFERENCED BY MAPPING, NEVER BY NUMERIC ID. OpenMRS concept_id values are",
    "install-specific - they depend on how CIEL was loaded - so the projector resolves every",
    "field with ConceptService.getConceptByMapping(code, source) at runtime.",
    "",
    "A field with an empty \"concept\" list is NOT YET CURATED: the projector skips it and",
    "reports it. Filling these in is a dictionary task, not a coding task - search your loaded",
    "CIEL for the concept named in \"name\", then add {\"source\": \"CIEL\", \"code\": \"<id>\"}.",
    "Ask for the coverage report (FhirProjectionRestController's GET) for the current count.",
    "",
    "The codes present were each verified against a public source: the CIEL vitals codes",
    "against openmrs-module-referenceapplication's own htmlforms/vitals.xml, and the LOINC",
    "codes against loinc.org. Nothing here was guessed.",
    "",
    "\"type\" must match what PatientviewDAOImpl actually puts in its map, and the projector",
    "refuses to write a value into a concept of an incompatible datatype rather than corrupt",
    "it - so a text-stored lab result mapped to a numeric concept is reported, not silently",
    "mangled."
  ],
  "encounterType": {
